{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 995016,
  "courseSlug": "vuejs-2-the-complete-guide",
  "courseTitle": "Vue - The Complete Guide (incl. Router & Composition API)",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "21463514",
      "title": "Defining & Validating Custom Events",
      "lectureOrder": 100,
      "videoOrder": 85,
      "sourceHash": "45d91147fdd6194f6db2e2e1e99f80fdb11abf7f21e737ddae26c0b6576bbb57",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.1,
          "end": 3.68,
          "en": "So as you can clearly tell",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 3.68,
          "end": 6.2,
          "en": "custom events are important,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.2,
          "end": 9.85,
          "en": "an important feature for a component communication.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 9.85,
          "end": 12.07,
          "en": "Now, just as with props,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 12.07,
          "end": 13.53,
          "en": "you can define them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 13.53,
          "end": 14.96,
          "en": "You can let Vue know",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 14.96,
          "end": 18.16,
          "en": "about the events your component will emit.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 18.16,
          "end": 20.69,
          "en": "For props, this is actually required.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 20.69,
          "end": 23.41,
          "en": "For events, it's recommended.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 23.41,
          "end": 26.69,
          "en": "Now I'll just close this here to gain some space.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 26.69,
          "end": 28.37,
          "en": "The props are still there,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 28.37,
          "end": 32.66,
          "en": "I'm just collapsing this so that it takes up less space.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 32.66,
          "end": 34.84,
          "en": "And I'll add a new property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 34.84,
          "end": 38.19,
          "en": "to the FriendContact configuration object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 38.19,
          "end": 40.403,
          "en": "And that's the emit property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 41.44,
          "end": 43.5,
          "en": "Now emits, so to say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 43.5,
          "end": 46.3,
          "en": "is the counterpart to props.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 46.3,
          "end": 47.7,
          "en": "In props you will define",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 47.7,
          "end": 49.89,
          "en": "which props this component receives.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 49.89,
          "end": 52.89,
          "en": "In emits, you will define which custom events",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 52.89,
          "end": 56.55,
          "en": "your component will eventually at some point emit.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 56.55,
          "end": 59.62,
          "en": "And you're doing this to document your component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 59.62,
          "end": 62.29,
          "en": "to make it obvious to other developers,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 62.29,
          "end": 64.05,
          "en": "how your component works,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 64.05,
          "end": 66.61,
          "en": "and to which events they can listen.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 66.61,
          "end": 68.01,
          "en": "This is simply useful.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 68.01,
          "end": 71.08,
          "en": "It makes it easier to understand your component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 71.08,
          "end": 74.5,
          "en": "Because otherwise I have to look through all your code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 74.5,
          "end": 76.72,
          "en": "to see that there is some code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 76.72,
          "end": 79.37,
          "en": "where you emit toggle-favorite.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 79.37,
          "end": 82.2,
          "en": "With emits, you would simply add",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 82.2,
          "end": 83.033,
          "en": "toggle",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 84.61,
          "end": 87.05,
          "en": "favorite here as a string to this disarray,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 87.05,
          "end": 88.4,
          "en": "and that would make it clear that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 88.4,
          "end": 91.53,
          "en": "there definitely is some code in your component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 91.53,
          "end": 95.303,
          "en": "which leads to an event with that identifier to be emitted.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 96.36,
          "end": 99.2,
          "en": "And you can also take emits to the next level.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 99.2,
          "end": 101.35,
          "en": "This is the basic form of using it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 101.35,
          "end": 105,
          "en": "and it already helps with understanding your component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 105,
          "end": 106.61,
          "en": "But just as with props,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 106.61,
          "end": 109.59,
          "en": "you can also specify an object instead,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 109.59,
          "end": 112.19,
          "en": "and then add your admitted events",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 112.19,
          "end": 115.12,
          "en": "as keys here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 115.12,
          "end": 116.75,
          "en": "like this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 116.75,
          "end": 120.61,
          "en": "and then provide a more detailed configuration.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 120.61,
          "end": 124.37,
          "en": "The configuration you should then add is a function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 124.37,
          "end": 127.2,
          "en": "a function that receives the data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 127.2,
          "end": 130.81,
          "en": "which you eventually will emit as parameters.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 130.81,
          "end": 132.05,
          "en": "So in this case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 132.05,
          "end": 134.27,
          "en": "we will eventually emit an ID.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 134.27,
          "end": 136.26,
          "en": "So here we would add",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 136.26,
          "end": 139.17000000000002,
          "en": "ID as a parameter,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 139.17000000000002,
          "end": 142.9,
          "en": "and I'm doing that to make it obvious that \"toggle-favorite\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 142.9,
          "end": 146.57,
          "en": "is an event that should be handled by a function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 146.57,
          "end": 148.28300000000002,
          "en": "that expects an ID.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 149.17000000000002,
          "end": 151.393,
          "en": "Because I will emit an ID here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 152.56,
          "end": 154.96,
          "en": "You can then also add validation here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 154.96,
          "end": 157.87,
          "en": "to make sure that when the event is emitted,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 157.87,
          "end": 160.67000000000002,
          "en": "this data, which should be part of the event",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 160.67000000000002,
          "end": 162.69,
          "en": "is not forgotten.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 162.69,
          "end": 166.23,
          "en": "We can check if ID exists,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 166.23,
          "end": 167.93,
          "en": "if this is true",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 167.93,
          "end": 170.59,
          "en": "and return true, if that's the case",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 170.59,
          "end": 173.61,
          "en": "and else return false,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 173.61,
          "end": 178.007,
          "en": "and maybe also issue a warning in the console that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 179.17000000000002,
          "end": 180.93,
          "en": "ID is missing,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 180.93,
          "end": 183.94,
          "en": "to help developers that are emitting this event,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 183.94,
          "end": 185.293,
          "en": "catch this error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 186.93,
          "end": 188,
          "en": "And now, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 188,
          "end": 190.46,
          "en": "if I remove this second argument here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 190.46,
          "end": 191.93,
          "en": "and I saved that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 191.93,
          "end": 193.87,
          "en": "and I click \"toggle-favorite\",",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 193.87,
          "end": 195.64,
          "en": "I get an error here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 195.64,
          "end": 197.32,
          "en": "But before that error,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 197.32,
          "end": 200.66,
          "en": "I actually also get a warning",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 200.66,
          "end": 202.46,
          "en": "invalid event arguments,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 202.46,
          "end": 205.88,
          "en": "event validation failed for event \"toggle-favorite\",",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 205.88,
          "end": 207.43,
          "en": "ID is missing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 207.43,
          "end": 209.8,
          "en": "So this is something which you don't have to add,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 209.8,
          "end": 213.24,
          "en": "but which can make your life as a developer easier,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 213.24,
          "end": 216.42000000000002,
          "en": "especially again if you're working in a team.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 216.42000000000002,
          "end": 218.32,
          "en": "Now let's bring this ID back",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 218.32,
          "end": 222.35,
          "en": "and I will not add this detailed of a validation",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 222.35,
          "end": 224.27,
          "en": "to the custom events throughout the course.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 224.27,
          "end": 225.67000000000002,
          "en": "But since it is the complete guide,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 225.67000000000002,
          "end": 227.7,
          "en": "I of course want to show this to you",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 227.7,
          "end": 229.303,
          "en": "so that you know this feature.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 230.48,
          "end": 232.81,
          "en": "Nonetheless, I will revert to this here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 232.81,
          "end": 235.2,
          "en": "and go back to this simpler definition,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 235.2,
          "end": 237.73,
          "en": "which is the approach I will use throughout the course",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 237.73,
          "end": 239.43,
          "en": "simply to make it obvious",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 239.43,
          "end": 243.393,
          "en": "which custom events this component will eventually emit.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
